Reflection and Self Assessment
Pradipta Dharmeswara
Issue 1: Double free
Initially my code caused a double free, despite my memory management seeming correct.
To fix this, I had to look at the test-mergesort.c file to make sure my frees lined up.
Thus, I changed from having each call free its own args to freeing the child args in the parent call.

Issue 2: Indexing
Sometimes my sort would fail, however this was inconsistent.
Although I could not test for this issue easily, it ended up being fixed when I double checked the indexing
for merge(). Initially I had each call sort into B[0], however with parallelisation this did not work out all the time
since two threads might end up writing into the same memory, which I suspect caused the sorting failures.

Daisy Rees
Issue 1: 
Paralell sort tried to access build arguments variables when they were implemented as local variables, and this did not work.
I had to alter the buildargs function to employ dynamic memory allocation so that the values were preserved across function calls.

Issue 2:
Although I had an understanding of the pthreads api, I had to combine this knowledge with my understanding of recursion to implement
recursive threading with the pthreads api. 


